{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1528249-ask-a-question-changeling-edition","id":1528249,"title":"Ask a Question, Changeling Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-09T02:48:50-08:00","id":1528249,"title":"Ask a Question, Changeling Edition","content":"I had a question about the game, and while I feel it is a waste to create a new thread for a single question. If I opened it up for anyone else to ask a question, that feel more worthwhile.<br /> <br /> My ridiculous, one-note question is this; what the rationale behind the Willpower restriction for House Balor's Frailty/Flaw? I don't understand how being a member of this House means that one cannot be determined to such an extent. Being adopted into the House will even <i>lower</i> new members Willpower ratings if they are above 6. And I can't think of a reason why, beyond maybe impulse control...which honestly could be covered by the Unseelie code, rather than Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T11:30:51-08:00","id":1528272,"title":"","content":"If there are any official statements that elaborate on the Willpower restriction beyond it being &quot;due to their savage Formorian blood&quot; (that's how it's phrased in C20 at least), then I'm not aware of them. I agree that attributing the Willpower cap to their Formorian origin in and of itself isn't really convincing: Thallain ties to the Formorians are at least as strong and they aren't limited in this way. If you're going by older editions of Changeling, it might make more sense to justify this part of the House Flaw in terms of the fact that half of their Seelie Legacies, arguably half of themselves, are so thoroughly shackled and silenced. An alternative explanation that could work for C20 <i>and</i> older editions would be that the cost of acquiring the House resistance to cold iron is a deadening of the self that makes it impossible to muster the sort of passion, commitment, and belief required to reach the highest levels of Willpower, but I'd generally expect that sort of thing to be expressed in terms of Banality.<br /> <br /> Or keeping the Formorian angle, maybe isn't so much that they have Formorian blood but that it wars against the fact that they are Kithain, splitting their focus even though they strongly favor their Formorian natures. Of course, this explanation wouldn't really work for a hypothetical Thallain member of the House; I know that they were being recruited in past editions, but it isn't clear if that means that any of them are members of the House proper as opposed to just oath-bound muscle.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't think it's a very good fit for this House made up of militaristic fanatics who have, for millennia, maintained a sense of identity and purpose that is actively antithetical to Kithain society as a whole despite being part of it at the same time, so I replaced it with something else. I don't recall if pre-C20 Changeling allowed violating a primary Legacy's Ban to be justified in terms of characteristics and tendencies associated with a secondary Legacy, but for C20 at least I think making it so that a Seelie Legacy can't ever be invoked to justify the violation of an Unseelie Legacy's Ban works as a fitting replacement for that part of the House Flaw; if there are Thallain members, then the arrangement would be that they can't justify violating the Taboos of their Nightmare Legacies in terms of their secondary Legacy, regardless of whether it's Unseelie or Seelie (though this obviously only works with C20 Thallain rules).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27894-paramecius","name":"Paramecius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27894_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T12:34:34-08:00","id":1528280,"title":"","content":"One big difference between House Balor and the Thallain is the Thallain were created by the Fomorians, while Balor are the children of the Fomorians and the Tuatha De Danann (or at least for the latter Balor sidhe are). Although part of it might be *which* Fomorians they're descended from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T17:03:17-08:00","id":1528289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1528249-ask-a-question-changeling-edition?p=1528280#post1528280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One big difference between House Balor and the Thallain is the Thallain were created by the Fomorians, while Balor are the children of the Fomorians and the Tuatha De Danann (or at least for the latter Balor sidhe are). Although part of it might be *which* Fomorians they're descended from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Birth/descent from vs creation is a fair point of distinction. I'm skeptical that the Fomorians would be weaker-willed than their minions, but maybe there's something to the notion that the House's limited Willpower has something to do with their ties to their namesake Fomorian, particularly in light of the fact that he was killed and his death/defeat was quite an unfavorable turning point in the history of the Fomorians in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27894-paramecius","name":"Paramecius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27894_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T17:37:29-08:00","id":1528291,"title":"","content":"Specifically Red Court could have lower Willpower sometimes I think. Much more so that White Court or Green Court at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T03:21:46-08:00","id":1528532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1528249-ask-a-question-changeling-edition?p=1528291#post1528291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically Red Court could have lower Willpower sometimes I think. Much more so that White Court or Green Court at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting interpretation. Though it does lead to a potentially amusing question; what are the Formorians?<br /> I do have an answer but it not canonical. I certainly can't tie it DA:F.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T05:32:36-08:00","id":1528539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1528249-ask-a-question-changeling-edition?p=1528532#post1528532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is an interesting interpretation. Though it does lead to a potentially amusing question; what are the Formorians?<br /> I do have an answer but it not canonical. I certainly can't tie it DA:F.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't tie anything to DA Fae either, and I don't think DA Fae canonically has anything to do with Changeling.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T10:19:05-08:00","id":1528548,"title":"","content":"There are hints in <b>C20</b> that <b>DA:Fae</b> <i>might</i> be the backstory for modern <b>Changeling</b>; and the final <b>Dark Ages</b> supplement <b>Darkening Sky</b> has a section for <b>DA:Fae</b> that triggers the Shattering. So I wouldn't go so far as to say that there's <i>no</i> canonical connection between the two. <br /> <br /> One of the writers of <b>C20</b> also wrote a Storyteller's Vault supplement called <b>Harbingers of Winter</b>. It has a whole chapter (Chapter Five: Waking Nightmares) talking about the Fomorians and their Courts (Green, Red, and White). The Fomorians themselves are presented as gods, and beyond the scope of what protagonists can confront directly, much like Rank 6+ spirits in <b>Werewolf</b>. But their Courts are populated by Thallain and Dark-Kin. Meanwhile, the Green, Red, and White Courts are presented as stepping stones between the Black Court and Kithain society. In effect, the Shadow Court is the other end of the progression. (The Black Court and the Shadow Court are talked about in Chapter Four.) Balor is described as a member of the Green Court. <br /> <br /> <b>Harbingers of Winter</b> also ties into the same author's Storyteller's Vault supplement for <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b> called <b>Past is Prologue</b> which details the Fomorians in that game's terms by adding a new Origin (Dark) and a Dominion of Nightmare, and to the same author's unofficial <b>C5</b>, which operates on the premise that Arcadia has fallen, the Fomorians (now known as the Elder Dark) have returned, the Endless Winter has begun, and the Dreaming is now hostile to changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T11:57:09-08:00","id":1528555,"title":"","content":"The problem is, the metaphysics of DA Fae are completely incompatible with Changeling the Dreaming, even if you do want to go with everything in Changeling history being a lie.<br /> <br /> Also, you really shouldn't listen to what authors say outside of the official published material when it comes to canonicity, it's irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T12:01:43-08:00","id":1528556,"title":"","content":"There are of course similarities between Changeling the Dreaming and DA Fae. There's also similarities between Changeling the Dreaming and Changeling the Lost. And yeah, DA Fae is in a historical setting for the World of Darkness. But the differences are too great for the fae in Changeling the Dreaming to be the descendants of the fae in DA Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T13:27:27-08:00","id":1528560,"title":"","content":"You said: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't tie anything to DA Fae either, and I don't think DA Fae canonically has anything to do with Changeling. </div> </div> </div>The first part is your prerogative, and incompatible metaphysics are a good argument for you to choose not to tie them together. The second part is arguably <i>not</i> true, whether or not the metaphysics are compatible. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, you really shouldn't listen to what authors say outside of the official published material when it comes to canonicity, it's irrelevant. </div> </div> </div>True enough. However, I wasn't bringing it up to reinforce the canonicity; I was only pointing it out to illustrates where the writer's head was at. It's also worth noting that the STV products that I pointed out arguably <i>might </i>have been canon if Paradox hadn't already pulled the plug on <b>Changeling</b>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are of course similarities between Changeling the Dreaming and DA Fae. There's also similarities between Changeling the Dreaming and Changeling the Lost. And yeah, DA Fae is in a historical setting for the World of Darkness. But the differences are too great for the fae in Changeling the Dreaming to be the descendants of the fae in DA Fae. </div> </div> </div>And again, that's your prerogative. It might even be the objectively right thing to do. It doesn't change the fact that there's evidence that the authorial intent is for <b>DA:Fae</b> to be the backstory for <b>CtD</b>; and saying that no such evidence exists takes things too far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T13:48:48-08:00","id":1528565,"title":"","content":"And again, authorial intent is irrelevant in the question of canonicity. It's the text that matters, not the things never put into the text, especially something with many authors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T15:26:41-08:00","id":1528570,"title":"","content":"Everything I mentioned was in text. Some of the text was arguably only \u201cunofficial\u201d because further official text had already been nixed by Paradox; but my argument doesn't <i>depend </i>on that text; it's just reinforced by it. The text in <b>Darkening Skies</b> is enough on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T16:47:29-08:00","id":1528574,"title":"","content":"Ok, I haven't read Darkening Skies, sorry. Does it also explain where the Dreaming was in DA Fae, and why suddenly Banality and Glamour became relevant to the fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T21:23:38-08:00","id":1528579,"title":"","content":"<b>Dark Ages: Fae</b> addresses the first part: in Chapter Six, it explores a series of options as to what the true nature of the fae might be; and on pages 197\u2013198, the option it addresses is \u201cDreams Incarnate\u201d. It outlined the possibility that the Fae and things associated with them, including the otherworldly realms they often inhabit, may in fact be created by human imagination, and that they just don't realize it. Though some suspect. <br /> <br /> The events of the Fae chapter of <b>Darkening Skies</b> describes what changes that. The story takes place, as do all of the stories in the book, during the eclipse of AD 1230, at the end of the Oath-Truce. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The story centers around a scheme to free a caravan of baptized changelings from the effects of baptism, allowing them to regain their full fae nature once again. At least, that's how it starts. In truth, the changelings in question are wearing Treasures that will kill them and release a new phenomen on the world, which is described in the book as a sort of \u201canti-magic\u201d field. Rumors of these Treasures spread throughout fae society, and the more warlike of the Fae start using them as weapons to devestate their enemies. What's really happening is that each baptized changeling's death creates a bit of Banality in the world</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The following is a direct quote from <b>Darkening Skies</b>, describing the long-term aftermath of the story:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Many fae who wish to rekindle the War of Seasons attempt to recreate it, causing more Unleashings all over and seeking out baptized changelings to cripple their enemies. More and more fae become Lost, and the Mists react violently to the abuse to the point that Unleashing becomes nearly impossible in some places, especially human cities. The firstborn find it more difficult to hide in the Mists and have to find other means to conceal themselves, if not retreat into faerie realms completely. Changelings feel the sting of this less keenly, as they can more naturally walk among humanity.<br /> <br /> In an effort to adapt, some fae try to use cantrips for the same effect of the Friar's Cross, especially changelings. With the imposition of order and structure, the fae themselves become less varied, taking on Features similar to one another that are shaped by the dreams and nightmares of humanity. This gives rise to different kiths of changelings.<br /> <br /> When the Oath-Truce falls, the Shattering begins.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's not particularly elegant, and many fans of both <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b> and <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> have criticized it for how kludgey it is. But one thing that nobody denies is that it's a deliberate effort to build a bridge from the former to the latter. <br /> <br /> <b>C20</b> then picks up the tale (pp.35\u201336): <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In 1230 an eclipse covered much of the Autumn world, but while that would pass unnoticed by far, this one also blotted out all light in the Dreaming. Panic over further human growth slowly spread in the courts. To protect themselves, many fae moved their holdings into the Dreaming to avoid contact with humanity, and the process acted to further sever bonds between the dream and the flesh. <br /> <br /> \u2026Over the course of the next two centuries, trods and freeholds vanished, were destroyed, or were otherwise lost to the fae. \u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026In the early 14th century, the Autumn world entered a new era that would eventually transition into the Renaissance. \u2026 </div></div> </div> </div><br /> The text then goes on to describe how the fae reacted, with some sealing themselves off in their freeholds and becoming the Lost Ones, others fleeing to what they now referred to as Arcadia, and the rest subjecting themselves to the newly discovered Changeling Way. <br /> <br /> By the end of the Shattering in the fifteenth century, the transition from <b>Fae</b> to <b>Changeling</b> metaphysics was complete. <br /> <br /> Which, incidentally, means that during the time of <b>Mage: the Sorcerers Crusade</b>, the world of the fae was smack dab in the most chaotic phase of the Shattering. At the start of the period, the Courts, Houses, and Kiths had already emerged, but the underlying metaphysics were likely still more like <b>Fae</b> than <b>Changeling</b>. By the end of it, all but two Houses had retreated from the Autumn world, and those who remained either became Lost Ones or Changelings; and the last of the true fae vanished from the face of the Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T23:19:09-08:00","id":1528782,"title":"","content":"Here's a question:<br /> <br /> When creating a chimerical companion, why would you spend 2 points on increasing weapon damage from strength+1 to strength+2 when you could spend the same 2 points to raise strength by 6?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T04:45:29-08:00","id":1531228,"title":"","content":"A question of my own.<br /> <br /> It is said that Gwydion the Grey himself was one of the few members of his House to stay behind on Earth during the Shattering. Now, imagine a scenario where it turns out he actually took to the Changeling Way, and an Autumn Sidhe of the House learns that he is his current incarnation. How would the rest of the House treat him? Would the joy of learning that their founder's soul has survived be soured by the fact that it was at the cost of becoming an Autumn Sidhe? Especially if the personality of the current incarnation doesn't match their image of the original?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T09:46:03-07:00","id":1535106,"title":"","content":"Can Changelings learn Inanimae Slivers?<br /> Also, do you need to pay glamour to unleash a Sliver even when the effect is Chimerical?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T10:57:42-07:00","id":1535108,"title":"","content":"No, changelings can't learn Slivers; and inanimae (other than mannikens) can't learn Arts. <br /> <br /> Unleashings always cost Glamour; that's part of how they work. You spend Glamour, and that helps determine how big of a dice pool you roll. <br /> <br /> And those two reasons are why Slivers <i>really</i> need cantrips.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-06T00:19:44-07:00","id":1535190,"title":"","content":"What is the maximum temporary banality you can shed through revelry? I can see it being either your permanent glamour or your (permanent - temporary) glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}